CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*vdev->region)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct vfio_platform_region)...)
#66: FILE: drivers/vfio/platform/vfio_platform.c:46:
+	vdev->region = kzalloc(sizeof(struct vfio_platform_region) * cnt,

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

